# CSS conventions

- Extend tokens in `@styles.css` `:root` — `--navy`, `--navy-dark`, `--navy-light`, `--gold`, `--off-white`, `--gray`, `--gray-light`, `--radius`, `--shadow`, `--transition`.
- Reuse existing component classes before inventing new ones.
- Prefer shared rules in `styles.css` over duplicating the same inline styles across pages.
- Avoid `!important` and avoid new global resets that fight the current base styles.
- Keep the mobile nav breakpoint aligned with JS (`768px`).
- Maintain navy/gold contrast for CTAs; primary buttons use gold, outline buttons stay light on dark sections.
